# Phase 5 — Multi-Step Workflow Chaining (DAG Pipeline)

## 🎯 What You Will Accomplish

Build the stateful Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) pipeline orchestrator. Sequence multi-step pipelines where steps execute only after upstream dependency steps succeed. Automatically pass outputs from parent steps as input arguments into dependent child steps.

---

## 💡 Core Concepts & Architecture Decisions

A Directed Acyclic Graph ensures tasks execute in strict topological dependency order with zero cycles. When a step completes, the orchestrator inspects the workflow: if all `dependsOn` steps for a child node are `COMPLETED`, the child step is enqueued immediately.

---

## 🛠 Step-by-Step Implementation

### Step 1 · DAG Step Resolution Engine
In `src/services/dagEngine.ts`:
```typescript
import { prisma } from "../lib/prisma";
import { workflowQueue } from "../queues/workflowQueue";

export class DagEngine {
  static async onStepCompleted(workflowId: string, completedStepId: string, output: any) {
    // 1. Mark step as completed
    await prisma.workflowStep.update({
      where: { id: completedStepId },
      data: { status: "COMPLETED", output }
    });

    // 2. Fetch all steps for this workflow
    const allSteps = await prisma.workflowStep.findMany({ where: { workflowId } });
    const completedStepNames = new Set(
      allSteps.filter((s) => s.status === "COMPLETED").map((s) => s.name)
    );

    // 3. Find pending steps whose dependencies are now 100% satisfied
    const readySteps = allSteps.filter((step) => {
      if (step.status !== "PENDING") return false;
      return step.dependsOn.every((dep) => completedStepNames.has(dep));
    });

    // 4. Enqueue ready steps concurrently
    for (const step of readySteps) {
      await workflowQueue.add("execute-step", {
        workflowId,
        stepId: step.id,
        stepName: step.name
      });
    }

    // 5. If all steps completed, mark workflow COMPLETED
    const allDone = allSteps.every((s) => s.status === "COMPLETED" || s.id === completedStepId);
    if (allDone) {
      await prisma.workflow.update({ where: { id: workflowId }, data: { status: "COMPLETED" } });
    }
  }
}
```

